{
  "primitive": "subject_collection_canonicalization",
  "description": "canonical_bytes(subject) for subject.collection/1 (verifier-toolkit/1 §8.5 + subject.collection/1 §7,§9): the UTF-8 bytes of the RFC 8785 (JCS) canonical serialization of the collection subject JSON value (exactly the four members of §7.6). subject_local_digest_hex = SHA3-256(canonical_bytes); the CCCP/1 commitment = SHA3-256(ASCII(nonce_hex) || ASCII(subject_local_digest_hex)) MUST equal the certificate's commitment_digest_hex. This pins the canonicalization of a collection subject in isolation (the merkle over its leaves is pinned separately by the collection-merkle primitive; the end-to-end pipeline by conformance/P007).",
  "profile": "subject.collection/1",
  "canonicalization": "rfc8785-jcs-utf8",
  "digest": "sha3-256",
  "nonce_hex": "abababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababab",
